{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"a46014a2f7b89cc33da4acd54806b4a9f0e13634242adc7a62e6a0117a29d60e","digest":{"component_or_area":"reconciler / apply handlers","key_entities":["apply_handlers.py","reconcile.py","RECONCILER_FAIL_SILENT_NOOP","comment_errors","mutation_failures","outcome[error]","acli_subprocess._check_mutation_failure","reconcile-bridge.yml","test_silent_noop_canary.py"],"problem_keywords":["silent no-op","reconciler failure","comment errors","fail-loud","observability","exit code","partial failures"],"propositions":["Silent sub-op failures (comment_errors) are recorded non-fatally and not counted in mutation_failures, allowing reconcile passes to exit 0 despite sync failures.","The RECONCILER_FAIL_SILENT_NOOP flag (default off) only applies to total no-ops, not partial comment drop failures.","Partial comment errors must be promoted to outcome[error] when RECONCILER_FAIL_SILENT_NOOP=1 to make them count toward mutation_failures and drive non-zero exit.","The silent-no-op canary coverage must include comments and labels validation, not just links.","Flag activation in reconcile-bridge.yml must be sequenced after Jira comment cleanup to avoid failing on legitimately-capped tickets."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787878472117020001,"uuid":"f2f64ed0-a42e-4bc8-884d-e34186871c8b"}